      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_67180f54ab628e68b2bc838f61148840799159fa2c80aef2270ba33d666d2b68",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Rather than forcing one endpoint asymptotic through the transition, the theorem retains lower-order oscillatory terms that can reorganize differently in different scale regimes. The detailed formula is a mediator between two coarse descriptions.",
