    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_e5adf8497b642f178b520ac654ec4dbbf617ce9a324a740484e5d9515c840685",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Fourier smoothing first converts the zero-pair statistic into mean squares of complementary prime Dirichlet sums. Their diagonal terms are controlled under RH, while the assumed uniform Twin Prime correlation converts frequency-shift off-diagonals into singular-series sums; the earlier centered cumulative discrepancy f then permits integration by parts that aligns and cancels terms from the two complementary ranges, leaving the transition formula's lower-order structure.",
